"""Approximate the component as a CJK punctuation/document-end detector.

Ideographic full stops and end-of-text markers give large positive
responses. Other fullwidth punctuation is weaker; commas and opening
parentheses can be negative. The punctuation table gives a settled value
and an extra response near document start. Han-heavy preceding text
amplifies CJK punctuation responses; merged newlines and quotes change
the full-stop value. Letter fractions and token counts reset at document
boundaries. Ordinary lexical tokens receive zero, leaving their smaller,
token-specific fluctuations unexplained.
