"""Detect I/i-like vowel tokens across scripts, with local spelling context.

Greek iota has the largest negative response, reduced in vowel pairs.
Latin and Cyrillic I-like letters respond more at word boundaries than
inside words. English auxiliary/conditional words also weaken spaced I.
Byte-fragment tokens are checked for newly completed i-like characters.
