Separate ] and 】 tokens fire strongly. Preceding punctuation usually
weakens a closer, except for escaped quotes. Empty [] pairs barely fire;
punctuation and line breaks bundled after ] usually suppress the response.
Ordinary words are left at zero. These are token shapes, not balanced syntax.
"""
READS = ()

SUFFIX_RESPONSE = {
    '(': 0.36, ',': 0.10, '.': 0.07, ':': 0.11,
    ')': 0.01, ';': 0.01, '[': 0.05, '\\': 0.22,
    '+': 0.34, '^': 0.28, '*': 0.25, '-': 0.17,
    '/': 0.17, '=': 0.09, '{': 0.23, '}': 0.16,
}


