"""Positive responses at the start of scoped names and after linking particles.

The strongest cases are names directly after :: and single Han characters
following the literary Chinese linker 之. Lowercase API names are stronger
than capitalized type names; factories, conversions, and tests are stronger
still. Member arrows, double-underscore names, and East Asian linking
particles have smaller responses. The estimates are coarse category means,
not an attempt to recognize which function will subsequently be called.
