"""layers.0.mlp.down_proj:4785 - fires on the word that follows a scope or genitive link.

Plain-language reading of when this component is active:
1. A name after the Rust/C++/PHP/Python path operator "::" (Vec::new, Box::new,
   serde_json::json, tests/test_x.py::test_y, std::cout). Constructor and function names
   such as "new", "json", "test", "create", "get", "fmt" fire strongly; other lower-case
   names fire moderately; capitalised type names fire weakly.
2. The Chinese classical genitive 之 ("of") followed by a noun character
   (吳楚之音, 不解之谜, 不正之风): strong. A 之 followed by punctuation is silent.
3. Weak activity after a few other connectives: "->" (member access), 而, の, 以, 为, 其.
Everything else is near zero.

The program looks only at the current token and the one before it (within a document).
"""
import unicodedata

