"""Approximate a response to encoded punctuation and message boundaries.

Large negative values mark chat endings, tool-call openings, hex/Unicode
escapes, and a few mojibake lead characters. Escapes and control characters
are more negative directly after letters. Ordinary quotes have a smaller
version of this effect. Chat-boundary responses grow with the available
within-document context; other ordinary text stays close to zero.

These are token-spelling rules, not a parser or an encoding detector.
